IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part II: incorporation (s 5 to s 14).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Who may incorporate, what the articles must say, the certificate, the
-- corporation's name, and a contract made before the corporation exists.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Each rule is named `<what it decides> within s <section>`. A fact that turns on the
-- regulations, on another Act, or on a section outside the cb1 range is a plain input named for the fact,
-- with a comment "out of range: section N (piece X)" at the input. A judgement the Act hands to the
-- Director or to a court (to exempt, to refuse, to order what it thinks fit) is an input, or the rule
-- returns what the Director may do and does not say what the Director will do.

§ `Part II -- Incorporation`

§§ `s 5 incorporators`

-- s 5(1): "One or more individuals or bodies corporate may incorporate a corporation by signing articles of
-- incorporation and complying with section 7." A signer who is neither an individual nor a body corporate
-- (a partnership, a trust) is not addressed by this subsection, so it is not counted (fork cb1-F1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:140 | 5 (1) One or more individuals or bodies corporate may incorporate a corporation by signing articles of incorporation and complying with section 7.
@ref CBCA s 5(1) incorporators (src:140)
GIVEN `the number of individuals who sign the articles of incorporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of bodies corporate that sign the articles of incorporation` IS A NUMBER
      `every individual who signs may incorporate under subsection 5(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signers have complied with section 7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the signers may incorporate a corporation within s 5(1)` MEANS
        (`the number of individuals who sign the articles of incorporation` PLUS `the number of bodies corporate that sign the articles of incorporation`) AT LEAST 1
    AND `every individual who signs may incorporate under subsection 5(2)`
    AND `the signers have complied with section 7`

-- s 5(2): an individual may incorporate "only if" the individual (a) is not less than 18 years of age;
-- (b) is not incapable; or (c) does not have the status of bankrupt. The text joins the three with "or";
-- read as alternatives, a 17-year-old who is neither incapable nor bankrupt would qualify, which defeats
-- paragraph (a). The three are read as cumulative (fork cb1-F3 in NOTES.md). "Incapable" is the keel's
-- definition (s 2(1)), called here with its three facts.
-- src:142 | (2) An individual may incorporate a corporation only if that individual
-- src:143 | (a) is not less than 18 years of age;
-- src:144 | (b) is not incapable; or
-- src:145 | (c) does not have the status of bankrupt.
@ref CBCA s 5(2) individuals (src:142-145)
GIVEN `the age of the individual in complete years` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual has been found, under the laws of a province, to be unable to manage their property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that inability is by reason of minority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has been declared incapable by a court in a jurisdiction outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has the status of bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual may incorporate a corporation within s 5(2)` MEANS
        `the age of the individual in complete years` AT LEAST 18
    AND (NOT (`incapable within s 2(1)`
                  `the individual has been found, under the laws of a province, to be unable to manage their property`
                  `that inability is by reason of minority`
                  `the individual has been declared incapable by a court in a jurisdiction outside Canada`))
    AND (NOT `the individual has the status of bankrupt`)

§§ `s 6 articles of incorporation`

-- The articles as the incorporators deliver them: one field per thing paragraph (a) to (f) asks them to
-- set out, and one for each condition that makes a requirement bite ("if there will be two or more
-- classes", "if a class may be issued in series", "if the issue, transfer or ownership of shares is to
-- be restricted"). A field that no condition makes necessary is still stated, as FALSE or TRUE.
-- src:147 | 6 (1) Articles of incorporation shall follow the form that the Director fixes and shall set out, in respect of the proposed corporation,
-- src:148 | (a) the name of the corporation;
-- src:149 | (b) the province in Canada where the registered office is to be situated;
-- src:150 | (c) the classes and any maximum number of shares that the corporation is authorized to issue, and
-- src:151 | (i) if there will be two or more classes of shares, the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to each class of shares, and
-- src:152 | (ii) if a class of shares may be issued in series, the authority given to the directors to fix the number of shares in, and to determine the designation of, and the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to, the shares of each series;
-- src:153 | (d) if the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of the corporation is to be restricted, a statement to that effect and a statement as to the nature of such restrictions;
-- src:154 | (e) the number of directors or, subject to paragraph 107(a), the minimum and maximum number of directors of the corporation; and
-- src:155 | (f) any restrictions on the businesses that the corporation may carry on.
@ref CBCA s 6(1) articles of incorporation (src:147-155)
DECLARE `Articles of incorporation as delivered (s 6(1))` HAS
    `follow the form that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set out the name of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set out the province in Canada where the registered office is to be situated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set out the classes and any maximum number of shares that the corporation is authorized to issue` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there will be two or more classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set out the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to each class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a class of shares may be issued in series` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set out the authority given to the directors to fix the number of shares in, and to determine the designation of, and the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to, the shares of each series` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of the corporation is to be restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set out a statement to that effect and a statement as to the nature of the restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set out the number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set out the minimum and maximum number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: section 107 (piece cb2)
    `paragraph 107(a) allows a minimum and maximum number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there are restrictions on the businesses that the corporation may carry on` IS A BOOLEAN
    `set out the restrictions on the businesses that the corporation may carry on` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:147 | 6 (1) Articles of incorporation shall follow the form that the Director fixes and shall set out, in respect of the proposed corporation,
-- src:148 | (a) the name of the corporation;
-- src:149 | (b) the province in Canada where the registered office is to be situated;
-- src:150 | (c) the classes and any maximum number of shares that the corporation is authorized to issue, and
-- src:151 | (i) if there will be two or more classes of shares, the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to each class of shares, and
-- src:152 | (ii) if a class of shares may be issued in series, the authority given to the directors to fix the number of shares in, and to determine the designation of, and the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to, the shares of each series;
-- src:153 | (d) if the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of the corporation is to be restricted, a statement to that effect and a statement as to the nature of such restrictions;
-- src:154 | (e) the number of directors or, subject to paragraph 107(a), the minimum and maximum number of directors of the corporation; and
-- src:155 | (f) any restrictions on the businesses that the corporation may carry on.
@ref CBCA s 6(1) articles of incorporation (src:147-155)
GIVEN articles IS AN `Articles of incorporation as delivered (s 6(1))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles of incorporation are complete within s 6(1)` articles MEANS
        articles's `follow the form that the Director fixes`
    AND articles's `set out the name of the corporation`                                                  -- (a)
    AND articles's `set out the province in Canada where the registered office is to be situated`         -- (b)
    AND articles's `set out the classes and any maximum number of shares that the corporation is authorized to issue`  -- (c)
    AND (    (NOT articles's `there will be two or more classes of shares`)                                -- (c)(i)
          OR articles's `set out the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to each class of shares`)
    AND (    (NOT articles's `a class of shares may be issued in series`)                                  -- (c)(ii)
          OR articles's `set out the authority given to the directors to fix the number of shares in, and to determine the designation of, and the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to, the shares of each series`)
    AND (    (NOT articles's `the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of the corporation is to be restricted`)   -- (d)
          OR articles's `set out a statement to that effect and a statement as to the nature of the restrictions`)
    AND (    articles's `set out the number of directors`                                                 -- (e)
          OR (    articles's `set out the minimum and maximum number of directors`
              AND articles's `paragraph 107(a) allows a minimum and maximum number of directors`))
    AND (    (NOT articles's `there are restrictions on the businesses that the corporation may carry on`)  -- (f)
          OR articles's `set out the restrictions on the businesses that the corporation may carry on`)

-- s 6(2): "The articles may set out any provisions permitted by this Act or by law to be set out in the
-- by-laws of the corporation."
-- src:157 | (2) The articles may set out any provisions permitted by this Act or by law to be set out in the by-laws of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 6(2) additional provisions in articles (src:157)
GIVEN `the provision is one that this Act or the law permits to be set out in the by-laws of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles may set out the provision within s 6(2)` MEANS
    `the provision is one that this Act or the law permits to be set out in the by-laws of the corporation`

-- s 6(4): the articles may not require a greater number of votes of shareholders to remove a director than
-- section 109 requires. Votes are fractions of the votes cast.
-- src:161 | (4) The articles may not require a greater number of votes of shareholders to remove a director than the number required by section 109.
@ref CBCA s 6(4) idem (src:161)
GIVEN `the fraction of the votes of shareholders that the articles require to remove a director` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: section 109 (piece cb2)
      `the fraction of the votes of shareholders that section 109 requires to remove a director` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an articles requirement for the removal of a director is permitted within s 6(4)` MEANS
    `the fraction of the votes of shareholders that the articles require to remove a director` AT MOST `the fraction of the votes of shareholders that section 109 requires to remove a director`

-- s 6(3): if the articles or a unanimous shareholder agreement require a greater number of votes than the
-- Act requires to effect an action, the articles or the agreement prevail, subject to s 6(4). Subsection
-- (4) limits only the articles: an agreement's higher requirement for the removal of a director is not
-- mentioned in it, so it is counted (fork cb1-F2). Where the articles' requirement for removal is barred by
-- (4), it counts for nothing and the Act's number stays.
-- src:159 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), if the articles or a unanimous shareholder agreement require a greater number of votes of directors or shareholders than that required by this Act to effect any action, the provisions of the articles or of the unanimous shareholder agreement prevail.
@ref CBCA s 6(3) special majorities (src:159)
GIVEN `the fraction of the votes that this Act requires to effect the action` IS A NUMBER
      `the fraction of the votes that the articles require` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the fraction of the votes that a unanimous shareholder agreement requires` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the action is the removal of a director by the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fraction of the votes needed to effect the action within s 6(3)` MEANS
    max `the fraction of the votes that this Act requires to effect the action`
        (max `what the articles add` `what the agreement adds`)
    WHERE
        `what the articles add` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the fraction of the votes that the articles require`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the fraction of the votes that this Act requires to effect the action`
            WHEN JUST required THEN
                IF `the action is the removal of a director by the shareholders`
                   AND (NOT (`an articles requirement for the removal of a director is permitted within s 6(4)` required `the fraction of the votes that this Act requires to effect the action`))
                THEN `the fraction of the votes that this Act requires to effect the action`
                ELSE required
        `what the agreement adds` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the fraction of the votes that a unanimous shareholder agreement requires`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the fraction of the votes that this Act requires to effect the action`
            WHEN JUST required THEN required

§§ `s 7 delivery of articles of incorporation`

-- "An incorporator shall send to the Director articles of incorporation and the documents required by
-- sections 19 and 106." Section 19 is in this piece (the notice of registered office, s 19(2)); section
-- 106 (the notice of directors) is not.
-- src:163 | 7 An incorporator shall send to the Director articles of incorporation and the documents required by sections 19 and 106.
@ref CBCA s 7 delivery of articles of incorporation (src:163)
GIVEN `the incorporator sent the articles of incorporation to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the incorporator sent the notice of registered office that section 19 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 106 (piece cb2)
      `the incorporator sent the notice of directors that section 106 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the incorporator has complied with the duty to send the articles and documents within s 7` MEANS
        `the incorporator sent the articles of incorporation to the Director`
    AND `the incorporator sent the notice of registered office that section 19 requires`
    AND `the incorporator sent the notice of directors that section 106 requires`

§§ `s 8 certificate of incorporation`

-- s 8(1): the Director "shall issue" the certificate on receipt of articles, subject to (2). s 8(2): the
-- Director "may refuse" if a notice under s 19(2) or s 106(1) indicates the corporation would not comply
-- with the Act. The Act gives the choice to refuse to the Director, so the rule says what the Director
-- must do or may do and does not say which the Director will choose. The form of the certificate is
-- governed by section 262 (out of range, piece cb5) and is not encoded.
-- src:165 | 8 (1) Subject to subsection (2), on receipt of articles of incorporation, the Director shall issue a certificate of incorporation in accordance with section 262.
-- src:167 | (2) The Director may refuse to issue the certificate if a notice that is required to be sent under subsection 19(2) or 106(1) indicates that the corporation, if it came into existence, would not be in compliance with this Act.
@ref CBCA s 8(1), s 8(2) certificate of incorporation (src:165 src:167)
DECLARE `Outcome of sending articles of incorporation under s 8` IS ONE OF
    `the Director must issue a certificate of incorporation`
    `the Director may either issue or refuse the certificate of incorporation`
    `no duty to issue a certificate arises because the Director has not received articles of incorporation`

-- src:165 | 8 (1) Subject to subsection (2), on receipt of articles of incorporation, the Director shall issue a certificate of incorporation in accordance with section 262.
-- src:167 | (2) The Director may refuse to issue the certificate if a notice that is required to be sent under subsection 19(2) or 106(1) indicates that the corporation, if it came into existence, would not be in compliance with this Act.
@ref CBCA s 8(1), s 8(2) certificate of incorporation (src:165 src:167)
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice required under subsection 19(2) or 106(1) indicates that the corporation, if it came into existence, would not be in compliance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 106(1) (piece cb2)
GIVETH A `Outcome of sending articles of incorporation under s 8`
`what the Director must or may do on receiving articles of incorporation within s 8` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Director has received articles of incorporation`)
            THEN `no duty to issue a certificate arises because the Director has not received articles of incorporation`
        IF `a notice required under subsection 19(2) or 106(1) indicates that the corporation, if it came into existence, would not be in compliance with this Act`
            THEN `the Director may either issue or refuse the certificate of incorporation`
        OTHERWISE `the Director must issue a certificate of incorporation`

§§ `s 9 effect of the certificate`

-- src:169 | 9 A corporation comes into existence on the date shown in the certificate of incorporation.
@ref CBCA s 9 effect of certificate (src:169)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of incorporation` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has come into existence by the day within s 9` MEANS
    day AT LEAST `the date shown in the certificate of incorporation`

§§ `s 10 name of corporation`

-- The words and abbreviations s 10(1) lists, in the text's order. The full forms are "Limited",
-- "Limitée", "Incorporated", "Incorporée", "Corporation" and "Société par actions de régime fédéral";
-- the abbreviations are "Ltd.", "Ltée", "Inc.", "Corp." and "S.A.R.F.". They are strings: a name is
-- checked by the words it contains.
-- src:171 | 10 (1) The word or expression “Limited”, “Limitée”, “Incorporated”, “Incorporée”, “Corporation” or “Société par actions de régime fédéral” or the corresponding abbreviation “Ltd.”, “Ltée”, “Inc.”, “Corp.” or “S.A.R.F.” shall be part, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense, of the name of every corporation, but a corporation may use and be legally designated by either the full or the corresponding abbreviated form.
@ref CBCA s 10(1) name of corporation (src:171)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the corporate words and abbreviations that s 10(1) lists` MEANS
    LIST "Limited", "Limitée", "Incorporated", "Incorporée", "Corporation", "Société par actions de régime fédéral",
         "Ltd.", "Ltée", "Inc.", "Corp.", "S.A.R.F."

-- "shall be part, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense, of the name of every
-- corporation". The input is the list of those words that the name contains in more than a figurative or
-- descriptive sense; a name that uses "Corporation" only as a description contributes nothing.
-- src:171 | 10 (1) The word or expression “Limited”, “Limitée”, “Incorporated”, “Incorporée”, “Corporation” or “Société par actions de régime fédéral” or the corresponding abbreviation “Ltd.”, “Ltée”, “Inc.”, “Corp.” or “S.A.R.F.” shall be part, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense, of the name of every corporation, but a corporation may use and be legally designated by either the full or the corresponding abbreviated form.
@ref CBCA s 10(1) name of corporation (src:171)
GIVEN `the corporate words the name contains, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporate name carries a required word within s 10(1)` MEANS
    any (GIVEN word YIELD elem word `the corporate words and abbreviations that s 10(1) lists`) `the corporate words the name contains, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense`

-- The second half of s 10(1): "a corporation may use and be legally designated by either the full or the
-- corresponding abbreviated form". The text lists six full forms and five abbreviations, in the same order
-- but with "Inc." once, so the pairing is a reading: "Incorporated" and "Incorporée" both take "Inc."
-- (fork cb1-F4 in NOTES.md). The privilege is the corporation's; no one else is given a right to object.
-- src:171 | 10 (1) The word or expression “Limited”, “Limitée”, “Incorporated”, “Incorporée”, “Corporation” or “Société par actions de régime fédéral” or the corresponding abbreviation “Ltd.”, “Ltée”, “Inc.”, “Corp.” or “S.A.R.F.” shall be part, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense, of the name of every corporation, but a corporation may use and be legally designated by either the full or the corresponding abbreviated form.
@ref CBCA s 10(1) name of corporation (src:171)
GIVEN `the full form` IS A STRING
      `the abbreviated form` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the abbreviated form corresponds to the full form within s 10(1)` MEANS
        (`the full form` EQUALS "Limited" AND `the abbreviated form` EQUALS "Ltd.")
    OR  (`the full form` EQUALS "Limitée" AND `the abbreviated form` EQUALS "Ltée")
    OR  (`the full form` EQUALS "Incorporated" AND `the abbreviated form` EQUALS "Inc.")
    OR  (`the full form` EQUALS "Incorporée" AND `the abbreviated form` EQUALS "Inc.")
    OR  (`the full form` EQUALS "Corporation" AND `the abbreviated form` EQUALS "Corp.")
    OR  (`the full form` EQUALS "Société par actions de régime fédéral" AND `the abbreviated form` EQUALS "S.A.R.F.")

-- src:171 | 10 (1) The word or expression “Limited”, “Limitée”, “Incorporated”, “Incorporée”, “Corporation” or “Société par actions de régime fédéral” or the corresponding abbreviation “Ltd.”, “Ltée”, “Inc.”, “Corp.” or “S.A.R.F.” shall be part, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense, of the name of every corporation, but a corporation may use and be legally designated by either the full or the corresponding abbreviated form.
@ref CBCA s 10(1) name of corporation (src:171)
GIVEN `the form the corporation uses` IS A STRING
      `the form the corporation has in its name` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may use and be legally designated by the form within s 10(1)` MEANS
        `the form the corporation uses` EQUALS `the form the corporation has in its name`
    OR  `the abbreviated form corresponds to the full form within s 10(1)` `the form the corporation has in its name` `the form the corporation uses`
    OR  `the abbreviated form corresponds to the full form within s 10(1)` `the form the corporation uses` `the form the corporation has in its name`

-- s 10(1) applies to every corporation, but (1.1) saves a corporation whose name included "Société
-- commerciale canadienne" or "S.C.C." immediately before the day subsection (1.1) came into force (the
-- day is not stated in the text: the fact is a plain input), and (2) lets the Director exempt a body
-- corporate continued under this Act. Whether the Director has exempted is the Director's choice: an input.
-- src:171 | 10 (1) The word or expression “Limited”, “Limitée”, “Incorporated”, “Incorporée”, “Corporation” or “Société par actions de régime fédéral” or the corresponding abbreviation “Ltd.”, “Ltée”, “Inc.”, “Corp.” or “S.A.R.F.” shall be part, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense, of the name of every corporation, but a corporation may use and be legally designated by either the full or the corresponding abbreviated form.
-- src:173 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply to a corporation that has a corporate name that, immediately before the day on which this subsection comes into force, included, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense, the expression “Société commerciale canadienne” or the abbreviation “S.C.C.”, and any such corporation may use and be legally designated by either that expression or that abbreviation.
-- src:175 | (2) The Director may exempt a body corporate continued as a corporation under this Act from the provisions of subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 10(1), s 10(1.1), s 10(2) name of corporation (src:171 src:173 src:175)
GIVEN `the name immediately before the day subsection 10(1.1) came into force included "Société commerciale canadienne" or "S.C.C." other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the day subsection 10(1.1) came into force (not in the text)
      `the body corporate was continued as a corporation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director has exempted the body corporate from subsection 10(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must carry a required word in its name within s 10(1), s 10(1.1) and s 10(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the name immediately before the day subsection 10(1.1) came into force included "Société commerciale canadienne" or "S.C.C." other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense`)
    AND (NOT (`the body corporate was continued as a corporation under this Act` AND `the Director has exempted the body corporate from subsection 10(1)`))

-- s 10(1.1), second half: such a corporation "may use and be legally designated by either that expression
-- or that abbreviation".
-- src:173 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply to a corporation that has a corporate name that, immediately before the day on which this subsection comes into force, included, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense, the expression “Société commerciale canadienne” or the abbreviation “S.C.C.”, and any such corporation may use and be legally designated by either that expression or that abbreviation.
@ref CBCA s 10(1.1) saving for S.C.C. (src:173)
GIVEN `the saving in subsection 10(1.1) applies to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expression or abbreviation` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may use and be legally designated by the expression or abbreviation within s 10(1.1)` MEANS
        `the saving in subsection 10(1.1) applies to the corporation`
    AND (`the expression or abbreviation` EQUALS "Société commerciale canadienne" OR `the expression or abbreviation` EQUALS "S.C.C.")

-- s 10(3): the name may be set out in the articles in an English form, a French form, an English form and
-- a French form, or a combined form, if the combined form meets the prescribed criteria (the regulations
-- are not among the sources); and the corporation may use and be legally designated by any such form.
-- Subject to s 12(1): a prohibited name is not allowed in any form.
-- src:177 | (3) Subject to subsection 12(1), the name of a corporation may be set out in its articles in an English form, a French form, an English form and a French form, or a combined English and French form, so long as the combined form meets the prescribed criteria. The corporation may use and may be legally designated by any such form.
@ref CBCA s 10(3) alternate name (src:177)
DECLARE `Form of corporate name set out in the articles (s 10(3))` IS ONE OF
    `an English form`
    `a French form`
    `an English form and a French form`
    `a combined English and French form`
    `any other form`

-- src:177 | (3) Subject to subsection 12(1), the name of a corporation may be set out in its articles in an English form, a French form, an English form and a French form, or a combined English and French form, so long as the combined form meets the prescribed criteria. The corporation may use and may be legally designated by any such form.
@ref CBCA s 10(3) alternate name (src:177)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of corporate name set out in the articles (s 10(3))`
      `the combined form meets the prescribed criteria` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the name is prohibited under subsection 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the form of name may be set out in the articles within s 10(3)` MEANS
        (NOT `the name is prohibited under subsection 12(1)`)
    AND CONSIDER form
        WHEN `an English form` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a French form` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an English form and a French form` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a combined English and French form` THEN `the combined form meets the prescribed criteria`
        WHEN `any other form` THEN FALSE

-- src:177 | (3) Subject to subsection 12(1), the name of a corporation may be set out in its articles in an English form, a French form, an English form and a French form, or a combined English and French form, so long as the combined form meets the prescribed criteria. The corporation may use and may be legally designated by any such form.
@ref CBCA s 10(3) alternate name (src:177)
GIVEN `the form of name may be set out in the articles under subsection 10(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is set out in the articles of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may use and be legally designated by the form within s 10(3)` MEANS
        `the form of name may be set out in the articles under subsection 10(3)`
    AND `the form is set out in the articles of the corporation`

-- s 10(4): for use outside Canada, any language form, subject to s 12(1).
-- src:179 | (4) Subject to subsection 12(1), a corporation may, for use outside Canada, set out its name in its articles in any language form and it may use and may be legally designated by any such form outside Canada.
@ref CBCA s 10(4) alternative name outside Canada (src:179)
GIVEN `the name is set out in the articles in a language form for use outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is prohibited under subsection 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may use and be legally designated by the name outside Canada within s 10(4)` MEANS
        `the name is set out in the articles in a language form for use outside Canada`
    AND `the use is outside Canada`
    AND (NOT `the name is prohibited under subsection 12(1)`)

-- s 10(5): the corporate name in legible characters in all contracts, invoices, negotiable instruments
-- and orders for goods or services "issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation".
-- src:181 | (5) A corporation shall set out its name in legible characters in all contracts, invoices, negotiable instruments and orders for goods or services issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 10(5) publication of name (src:181)
DECLARE `Kind of document under s 10(5)` IS ONE OF
    `a contract issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation`
    `an invoice issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation`
    `a negotiable instrument issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation`
    `an order for goods or services issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation`
    `any other document`

-- src:181 | (5) A corporation shall set out its name in legible characters in all contracts, invoices, negotiable instruments and orders for goods or services issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 10(5) publication of name (src:181)
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Kind of document under s 10(5)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must set out its name in legible characters on the document within s 10(5)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the document`
    WHEN `a contract issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an invoice issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a negotiable instrument issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an order for goods or services issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other document` THEN FALSE

-- src:181 | (5) A corporation shall set out its name in legible characters in all contracts, invoices, negotiable instruments and orders for goods or services issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 10(5) publication of name (src:181)
GIVEN `the corporation must set out its name on the document under subsection 10(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation's name is set out in legible characters on the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has complied with the duty to set out its name within s 10(5)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation must set out its name on the document under subsection 10(5)`)
    OR  `the corporation's name is set out in legible characters on the document`

-- s 10(6): another name for business is allowed if it does not contain, other than in a figurative or
-- descriptive sense, any of the s 10(1) words or abbreviations; subject to s 10(5) (the corporate name
-- still has to appear on the documents) and s 12(1).
-- src:183 | (6) Subject to subsections (5) and 12(1), a corporation may carry on business under or identify itself by a name other than its corporate name if that other name does not contain, other than in a figurative or descriptive sense, either the word or expression “Limited”, “Limitée”, “Incorporated”, “Incorporée”, “Corporation” or “Société par actions de régime fédéral” or the corresponding abbreviation.
@ref CBCA s 10(6) other name (src:183)
GIVEN `the corporate words the other name contains, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `the other name is prohibited under subsection 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may carry on business under or identify itself by the other name within s 10(6)` MEANS
        (NOT (any (GIVEN word YIELD elem word `the corporate words and abbreviations that s 10(1) lists`) `the corporate words the other name contains, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense`))
    AND (NOT `the other name is prohibited under subsection 12(1)`)

§§ `s 11 reserving a name; designating number`

-- s 11(1): the Director "may, on request, reserve for a prescribed period" a name for an intended
-- corporation or for a corporation that intends to change its name. Whether the Director reserves it is
-- the Director's choice; the rule says whether the Director may. The period is prescribed (not among the
-- sources), so it is an input in whatever unit the regulations use.
-- src:185 | 11 (1) The Director may, on request, reserve for a prescribed period a name for an intended corporation or for a corporation that intends to change its name.
@ref CBCA s 11(1) reserving name (src:185)
GIVEN `a request has been made to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is for an intended corporation or for a corporation that intends to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may reserve the name within s 11(1)` MEANS
        `a request has been made to the Director`
    AND `the name is for an intended corporation or for a corporation that intends to change its name`

-- src:185 | 11 (1) The Director may, on request, reserve for a prescribed period a name for an intended corporation or for a corporation that intends to change its name.
@ref CBCA s 11(1) reserving name (src:185)
GIVEN `the day the name is reserved` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed period of reservation` IS A `Time limit`   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the name stays reserved within s 11(1)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the prescribed period of reservation` `counted from` `the day the name is reserved`

-- s 11(2): "If requested to do so by the incorporators or a corporation, the Director shall assign ... as
-- its name a designating number followed by the word 'Canada' and a word or expression, or the
-- corresponding abbreviation, referred to in subsection 10(1)."
-- src:187 | (2) If requested to do so by the incorporators or a corporation, the Director shall assign to the corporation as its name a designating number followed by the word “Canada” and a word or expression, or the corresponding abbreviation, referred to in subsection 10(1).
@ref CBCA s 11(2) designating number (src:187)
GIVEN `the incorporators have requested a designating number name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has requested a designating number name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must assign a designating number name within s 11(2)` MEANS
        `the incorporators have requested a designating number name`
    OR  `the corporation has requested a designating number name`

-- src:187 | (2) If requested to do so by the incorporators or a corporation, the Director shall assign to the corporation as its name a designating number followed by the word “Canada” and a word or expression, or the corresponding abbreviation, referred to in subsection 10(1).
@ref CBCA s 11(2) designating number (src:187)
GIVEN `the name is a designating number followed by the word "Canada"` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word or expression that follows the word "Canada"` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the name is a designating number name within s 11(2)` MEANS
        `the name is a designating number followed by the word "Canada"`
    AND elem `the word or expression that follows the word "Canada"` `the corporate words and abbreviations that s 10(1) lists`

§§ `s 12 prohibited names; directing a change of name`

-- "a name that is prohibited by the regulations or that does not meet the prescribed requirements". The
-- regulations are not among the sources; both facts are plain inputs.
-- src:189 | 12 (1) A corporation shall not be incorporated or continued as a corporation under this Act with, change its name to, or have, carry on business under or identify itself by a name that is prohibited by the regulations or that does not meet the prescribed requirements.
@ref CBCA s 12(1) prohibited names (src:189)
GIVEN `the name is prohibited by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the name meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the name is prohibited within s 12(1)` MEANS
        `the name is prohibited by the regulations`
    OR  (NOT `the name meets the prescribed requirements`)

-- s 12(2): the Director "may direct" a change of name in accordance with s 173 (out of range, piece cb4)
-- if the corporation, "through inadvertence or otherwise", acquires a prohibited name.
-- src:191 | (2) The Director may direct a corporation to change its name in accordance with section 173 if, through inadvertence or otherwise, the corporation acquires a name that is prohibited by the regulations or that does not meet the prescribed requirements.
@ref CBCA s 12(2) directing change of name (src:191)
GIVEN `the corporation has acquired a name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is prohibited by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the name meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may direct the corporation to change its name within s 12(2)` MEANS
        `the corporation has acquired a name`
    AND `the name is prohibited within s 12(1)` `the name is prohibited by the regulations` `the name meets the prescribed requirements`

-- src:194 | (4) If a corporation has a designating number as its name, the Director may direct the corporation to change its name to a name other than a designating number in accordance with section 173.
@ref CBCA s 12(4) idem (src:194)
GIVEN `the corporation has a designating number as its name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may direct the corporation to change a designating number name within s 12(4)` MEANS
    `the corporation has a designating number as its name`

-- s 12(4.1): a name acquired through someone's undertaking to dissolve or to change names that is not
-- honoured: the Director may direct a change "unless the undertaking is honoured within the period
-- specified in subsection (5)" (the prescribed period). That period is not given in the text, so whether
-- the undertaking was honoured within it is a plain input.
-- src:196 | (4.1) Where a corporation acquires a name as a result of a person undertaking to dissolve or to change names, and the undertaking is not honoured, the Director may direct the corporation to change its name in accordance with section 173, unless the undertaking is honoured within the period specified in subsection (5).
@ref CBCA s 12(4.1) undertaking to change name (src:196)
GIVEN `the corporation acquired its name as a result of a person undertaking to dissolve or to change names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking was honoured within the period specified in subsection 12(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may direct the corporation to change its name because an undertaking was not honoured within s 12(4.1)` MEANS
        `the corporation acquired its name as a result of a person undertaking to dissolve or to change names`
    AND (NOT `the undertaking was honoured within the period specified in subsection 12(5)`)

-- s 12(5): if the corporation has not followed a directive under (2), (4) or (4.1) within the prescribed
-- period, the Director "may revoke" its name and assign one; until changed under s 173 the corporation's
-- name is the name the Director assigned.
-- src:198 | (5) If a corporation has not followed a directive under subsection (2), (4) or (4.1) within the prescribed period, the Director may revoke the name of the corporation and assign a name to it and, until changed in accordance with section 173, the name of the corporation is the name assigned by the Director.
@ref CBCA s 12(5) revoking name (src:198)
GIVEN `the Director has directed the corporation to change its name under subsection 12(2), (4) or (4.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has followed the directive within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may revoke the corporation's name and assign a name within s 12(5)` MEANS
        `the Director has directed the corporation to change its name under subsection 12(2), (4) or (4.1)`
    AND (NOT `the corporation has followed the directive within the prescribed period`)

-- src:198 | (5) If a corporation has not followed a directive under subsection (2), (4) or (4.1) within the prescribed period, the Director may revoke the name of the corporation and assign a name to it and, until changed in accordance with section 173, the name of the corporation is the name assigned by the Director.
@ref CBCA s 12(5) revoking name (src:198)
GIVEN `the day of the directive` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed period for following the directive` IS A `Time limit`   -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the corporation to follow the directive within s 12(5)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the prescribed period for following the directive` `counted from` `the day of the directive`

-- src:198 | (5) If a corporation has not followed a directive under subsection (2), (4) or (4.1) within the prescribed period, the Director may revoke the name of the corporation and assign a name to it and, until changed in accordance with section 173, the name of the corporation is the name assigned by the Director.
@ref CBCA s 12(5) revoking name (src:198)
GIVEN `the name of the corporation before the revocation` IS A STRING
      `the Director has revoked the name and assigned a name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name assigned by the Director` IS A STRING
      `the name has since been changed in accordance with section 173` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 173 (piece cb4)
      `the name the corporation changed it to` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the name of the corporation within s 12(5)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Director has revoked the name and assigned a name`) THEN `the name of the corporation before the revocation`
        IF `the name has since been changed in accordance with section 173` THEN `the name the corporation changed it to`
        OTHERWISE `the name assigned by the Director`

§§ `s 13 certificate of amendment after a revocation`

-- s 13(1): "the Director shall issue a certificate of amendment showing the new name ... and shall give
-- notice of the change of name as soon as practicable in a publication generally available to the public".
-- src:200 | 13 (1) When a corporation has had its name revoked and a name assigned to it under subsection 12(5), the Director shall issue a certificate of amendment showing the new name of the corporation and shall give notice of the change of name as soon as practicable in a publication generally available to the public.
@ref CBCA s 13(1) certificate of amendment (src:200)
GIVEN `the corporation has had its name revoked and a name assigned to it under subsection 12(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of amendment and give notice of the new name within s 13(1)` MEANS
    `the corporation has had its name revoked and a name assigned to it under subsection 12(5)`

-- src:202 | (2) The articles of the corporation are amended accordingly on the date shown in the certificate of amendment.
@ref CBCA s 13(2) effect of certificate (src:202)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles are amended by the certificate of amendment by the day within s 13(2)` MEANS
    day AT LEAST `the date shown in the certificate of amendment`

§§ `s 14 contracts made before the corporation exists`

-- s 14(1): "a person who enters into, or purports to enter into, a written contract in the name of or on
-- behalf of a corporation before it comes into existence is personally bound by the contract and is
-- entitled to its benefits", "subject to this section".
-- src:204 | 14 (1) Subject to this section, a person who enters into, or purports to enter into, a written contract in the name of or on behalf of a corporation before it comes into existence is personally bound by the contract and is entitled to its benefits.
@ref CBCA s 14(1) personal liability (src:204)
GIVEN `the contract is written` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person entered into or purported to enter into it in the name of or on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation had not yet come into existence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is personally bound by the pre-incorporation contract at the outset within s 14(1)` MEANS
        `the contract is written`
    AND `the person entered into or purported to enter into it in the name of or on behalf of the corporation`
    AND `the corporation had not yet come into existence`

-- s 14(2): the corporation may, "within a reasonable time after it comes into existence, by any action or
-- conduct signifying its intention to be bound", adopt a written contract made before it came into
-- existence in its name or on its behalf; on adoption (a) the corporation is bound and entitled as if it
-- had been a party at the date of the contract, and (b) the person ceases, "except as provided in
-- subsection (3)", to be bound or entitled. Whether the time was reasonable is a judgement for a court
-- and is an input.
-- src:206 | (2) A corporation may, within a reasonable time after it comes into existence, by any action or conduct signifying its intention to be bound thereby, adopt a written contract made before it came into existence in its name or on its behalf, and on such adoption
@ref CBCA s 14(2) pre-incorporation and pre-amalgamation contracts (src:206)
GIVEN `the contract is written and was made before the corporation came into existence in its name or on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation acted or conducted itself so as to signify its intention to be bound` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that was within a reasonable time after the corporation came into existence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has adopted the contract within s 14(2)` MEANS
        `the contract is written and was made before the corporation came into existence in its name or on its behalf`
    AND `the corporation acted or conducted itself so as to signify its intention to be bound`
    AND `that was within a reasonable time after the corporation came into existence`

-- s 14(4): "If expressly so provided in the written contract, a person who purported to act in the name of
-- or on behalf of the corporation before it came into existence is not in any event bound by the contract
-- or entitled to the benefits thereof." (3) is subject to it.
-- src:212 | (4) If expressly so provided in the written contract, a person who purported to act in the name of or on behalf of the corporation before it came into existence is not in any event bound by the contract or entitled to the benefits thereof.
@ref CBCA s 14(4) exemption from personal liability (src:212)
GIVEN `the written contract expressly provides that the person is not bound by it or entitled to its benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is exempt from the contract within s 14(4)` MEANS
    `the written contract expressly provides that the person is not bound by it or entitled to its benefits`

-- s 14(3): a party to the written contract may apply to a court for an order respecting the nature and
-- extent of the obligations and liability of the corporation and the person, "whether or not" the
-- contract was adopted; the court "may make any order it thinks fit" (a discretion the Act gives to the
-- court: the rule says whether the court may make an order, never what it will order). Subject to (4).
-- src:210 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), whether or not a written contract made before the coming into existence of a corporation is adopted by the corporation, a party to the contract may apply to a court for an order respecting the nature and extent of the obligations and liability under the contract of the corporation and the person who entered into, or purported to enter into, the contract in the name of or on behalf of the corporation. On the application, the court may make any order it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 14(3) application to court (src:210)
GIVEN `the contract is written and was made before the corporation came into existence in its name or on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a party may apply to a court for an order within s 14(3)` MEANS
        `the contract is written and was made before the corporation came into existence in its name or on its behalf`
    AND `the applicant is a party to the contract`

-- src:210 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), whether or not a written contract made before the coming into existence of a corporation is adopted by the corporation, a party to the contract may apply to a court for an order respecting the nature and extent of the obligations and liability under the contract of the corporation and the person who entered into, or purported to enter into, the contract in the name of or on behalf of the corporation. On the application, the court may make any order it thinks fit.
-- src:212 | (4) If expressly so provided in the written contract, a person who purported to act in the name of or on behalf of the corporation before it came into existence is not in any event bound by the contract or entitled to the benefits thereof.
@ref CBCA s 14(3), s 14(4) application to court, exemption (src:210 src:212)
GIVEN `a party may apply to a court under subsection 14(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempt from the contract under subsection 14(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make an order about the obligations of the person within s 14(3)` MEANS
        `a party may apply to a court under subsection 14(3)`
    AND (NOT `the person is exempt from the contract under subsection 14(4)`)

-- The position of the person who signed, after all four subsections. Bound at the outset (1), unless
-- exempt by the contract (4); on adoption the person ceases to be bound (2)(b) "except as provided in
-- subsection (3)", that is, unless a court order under (3) makes them bound. A court order cannot
-- override (4): (3) is subject to (4).
-- src:204 | 14 (1) Subject to this section, a person who enters into, or purports to enter into, a written contract in the name of or on behalf of a corporation before it comes into existence is personally bound by the contract and is entitled to its benefits.
-- src:208 | (b) a person who purported to act in the name of or on behalf of the corporation ceases, except as provided in subsection (3), to be bound by or entitled to the benefits of the contract.
-- src:210 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), whether or not a written contract made before the coming into existence of a corporation is adopted by the corporation, a party to the contract may apply to a court for an order respecting the nature and extent of the obligations and liability under the contract of the corporation and the person who entered into, or purported to enter into, the contract in the name of or on behalf of the corporation. On the application, the court may make any order it thinks fit.
-- src:212 | (4) If expressly so provided in the written contract, a person who purported to act in the name of or on behalf of the corporation before it came into existence is not in any event bound by the contract or entitled to the benefits thereof.
@ref CBCA s 14(1), s 14(2)(b), s 14(3), s 14(4) personal liability, helper (src:204 src:208 src:210 src:212)
GIVEN `the person is bound at the outset under subsection 14(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has adopted the contract under subsection 14(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempt from the contract under subsection 14(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has ordered under subsection 14(3) that the person is bound` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is personally bound by and entitled to the benefits of the contract within s 14` MEANS
        `the person is bound at the outset under subsection 14(1)`
    AND (NOT `the person is exempt from the contract under subsection 14(4)`)
    AND (    (NOT `the corporation has adopted the contract under subsection 14(2)`)
          OR `a court has ordered under subsection 14(3) that the person is bound`)

-- src:207 | (a) the corporation is bound by the contract and is entitled to the benefits thereof as if the corporation had been in existence at the date of the contract and had been a party thereto; and
@ref CBCA s 14(2)(a) pre-incorporation and pre-amalgamation contracts (src:207)
GIVEN `the corporation has adopted the contract under subsection 14(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is bound by and entitled to the benefits of the contract as if it had been a party from the date of the contract within s 14(2)(a)` MEANS
    `the corporation has adopted the contract under subsection 14(2)`
